---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
---

<Base title="About" description={`About ${SITE.name}: research across software security, quantitative finance and machine learning.`}>
  <article class="prose">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>{SITE.name}</h1>
      <p class="lede">I'm a researcher working across software security, quantitative finance and machine learning. Online I go by <code>{SITE.handle}</code>.</p>
    </header>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Reverse engineering and software protection:</strong> .NET internals, obfuscators and code virtualizers, anti-tamper and licensing schemes.</li>
      <li><strong>Offensive security:</strong> authorized penetration testing, web application security and Windows internals.</li>
      <li><strong>Malware analysis and incident response.</strong></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Flaws I find in third-party products are reported to the vendor first. Published results are on the <a href="/advisories/">advisories</a> page.</p>

    <h2>Quantitative finance</h2>
    <p>Systematic trading research: strategy design, backtesting and evaluation.</p>

    <h2>Machine learning and AI</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Machine learning projects</strong>, including models for the quantitative work above.</li>
      <li><strong>AI-assisted security research:</strong> agent-driven analysis pipelines with verifiable, provenance-checked output.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>I only test what I'm authorized to test, with a written scope.</li>
      <li>Client findings stay with the client. Product-level flaws go to the vendor through <a href="/disclosure-policy/">coordinated disclosure</a>.</li>
      <li>Public write-ups never include client-identifying details or working exploits for unfixed issues.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Work with me</h2>
    <p>I take on authorized protection assessments and security audits. The <a href="/services/">services page</a> explains what I offer and how an engagement runs. For everything else, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
